[0.000, "o", "--------\r\n\u001b[36muser\u001b[0m\r\nUse $sams-tree to organize this material into a scannable tree.\r\n\r\n<stdin>\r\n# Planning notes: Trailhead app (synthetic demo input)\r\n\r\nThese notes are invented for a skill demo. Trailhead is not a real product.\r\n\r\n- Onboarding: welcome screen copy is done. Account creation form needs password rules.\r\n  Permissions prompt for location still shows too early, move it after the first map view.\r\n- Map screen: offline tiles load slowly on older phones. Trail markers overlap when zoomed out.\r\n  Add a filter for difficulty (easy, moderate, hard).\r\n- Trail detail: photos carousel works. Elevation chart is missing units.\r\n  Reviews tab lists newest first; sort by helpful is requested.\r\n- Saved trails: sync between phone and tablet drops items saved offline.\r\n- Settings: units toggle (miles/km), notification preferences, delete account flow (legal review pending).\r\n- Release: beta build goes to 40 testers. App Store screenshots need the new map style.\r\n  Privacy label must mention location use.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "</stdin>\r\n"]
[5.565, "o", "\u001b[35m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[3"]
[0.000, "o", "mcodex\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\nI’ll use the sams-tree skill to group the notes by screen and release work.\r\n"]
[1.319, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[3mexec\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /private/tmp/skills-demo-sams-tree/home/.agents/skills/sams-tree/SKILL.md /private/tmp/skills-demo-sams-tree/home/.agents/skills/sams-tree/references/tree-format.md'\u001b[0m in /private/tmp/skills-demo-sams-tree/home/sams-tree-demo"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[32m succeeded in 0ms:\u001b[0m\r\n---\r\nname: sams-tree\r\ndescription: Organize supplied or established material into a familiar, scannable plain-text tree. Use for tree views of notes, topics, plans, or work, without adding project-status investigation.\r\n---\r\n\r\n# Sam's Tree\r\n\r\nMake a large amount of information easy to scan without making the reader learn a new organization. Every tree must combine branch connectors, short labels, and a meaningful emoji or visual marker on each row; plain unmarked labels are not the default.\r\n\r\nUse the subject and scope established by the prompt and conversation. Read [the tree format](references/tree-format.md), which this skill owns. Render the tree directly when the material is sufficient; ask only when an essential scope or relationship cannot be inferred.\r\n\r\n## Organize Familiar Material\r\n\r\n- Keep known names and groupings. Infer obvious relationships from the supplied material, but do not silently invent categories or factual relationships.\r\n- Preserve an explicitly requested"]
[0.000, "o", " hierarchy. Otherwise choose the structure the reader is most likely to recognize.\r\n- For interactive products, prefer known navigation and screens. If those are unavailable, use the team's familiar internal work hierarchy. For other subjects, use their established organization.\r\n- When useful, suggest up to three simple new grouping names after the tree. Show names only, separately from the existing structure. Zero suggestions is valid.\r\n\r\n## Scope and Detail\r\n\r\nDefault to three displayed levels beneath an implied subject or project. Collapse non-relevant branches, retaining their names so the reader can ask to expand them. Compress deeper familiar paths with `->`, preserving the original names and order.\r\n\r\nThe user may request more levels or expand a branch. Keep the rest of the view stable unless the new request changes its scope.\r\n\r\nWork from available material. A tree request does not require searching connected trackers, assigning work statuses, or changing source records. For a project status request,"]
[0.000, "o", " use `sams-status` when available; this skill remains usable on its own.\r\n# Tree Format\r\n\r\nThis presentation contract is owned by `sams-tree`. An identical bundled copy in `sams-status` lets either skill install independently. Keep both copies aligned when changing the collection.\r\n\r\n- Use a fenced `text` block with Unicode branches such as `├──`, `│`, and `└──`. Keep one short item per line and align connector columns.\r\n- Prefix every item label with a meaningful emoji or visual marker so branches and leaves are easy to scan. Use consistent category markers such as 📁 for groups and 📄 for items when no more useful subject-specific marker is evident.\r\n- For work-status trees, use the established status symbol as the row marker rather than stacking decorative icons. For ordinary trees, category markers do not imply progress or completion.\r\n- If the user requests no emoji or the output medium cannot render them, use compact text markers such as `[group]` and `[item]`, retaining the branching "]
[0.000, "o", "and indentation. An explicit request for a different format takes precedence.\r\n- Leave the subject or project implied, outside the tree's counted levels. A short introductory line may disambiguate it.\r\n- Show at most three displayed levels by default. The first visible items are level one. Honor requests for more detail.\r\n- Use known or easily inferred names and groupings. Combine deeper known paths with `->`, retaining their names and order.\r\n- Collapse non-relevant branches by showing their name followed by `…`. The ellipsis means hidden detail, not missing or completed work. Expand on request.\r\n- Preserve sibling order from the familiar source hierarchy when known. Prefer short labels over sentence-length descriptions.\r\n- Put helpful source IDs beside the items they support. Below the block, provide clickable links keyed by those IDs. Reuse one link per source; keep URLs outside the tree. Never invent IDs or links.\r\n- If useful, add up to three simple proposed grouping names outside the tree. Do not appl"]
[0.000, "o", "y those new groupings without a user request.\r\n\r\n`sams-status` defines the work-status and freshness vocabulary. Add a compact legend only when a marker’s meaning is not obvious or already established.\r\n\r\n"]
[7.586, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[3mcodex\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\nTrailhead app — planning notes (synthetic demo)\r\n\r\n```text\r\n├── 🚪 Onboarding\r\n│   ├── 📝 Welcome screen copy: done\r\n│   ├── 🔐 Account creation: add password rules\r\n│   └── 📍 Location prompt: move after first map view\r\n├── 🗺️ Map screen\r\n│   ├── 📱 Offline tiles: slow on older phones\r\n│   ├── 📌 Trail markers: overlap when zoomed out\r\n│   └── 🔎 Add difficulty filter: easy, moderate, hard\r\n├── 🥾 Trail detail\r\n│   ├── 🖼️ Photos carousel: works\r\n│   ├── 📈 Elevation chart: add missing units\r\n│   └── 💬 Reviews\r\n│       ├── 📅 Current sort: newest first\r\n│       └── 👍 Requested sort: helpful\r\n├── 🔖 Saved trails\r\n│   └── 🔄 Phone–tablet sync: drops trails saved offline\r\n├── ⚙️ Settings\r\n│   ├── 📏 Units toggle: miles/km\r\n│   ├── 🔔 Notification preferences\r\n│   └── 🗑️ Delete account "]
[0.000, "o", "flow: legal review pending\r\n└── 🚀 Release\r\n    ├── 🧪 Beta build: 40 testers\r\n    ├── 🖼️ App Store screenshots: use new map style\r\n    └── 🔏 Privacy label: mention location use\r\n```"]
